{#
  Base layout: the frame every page sits in.

  Pages supply content and front matter only. They never restate the shell, and
  they never rebuild the masthead or footer. This is the frame half of the
  frame-plus-blocks model; the components in _includes/components are the
  blocks.
#}<!doctype html>
{# lang is hardcoded: this site is English only by decision, so there is no
   per-page locale override to honour. See SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md. #}
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>{{ title or site.title }}</title>
  <meta name="description" content="{{ deck or description or site.description }}">

  {# Self-referencing canonical on every page, from the same absoluteUrl filter
     partials/schema.njk builds its @id with, so the two cannot name different
     URLs. Self-referencing is the point: it is not there to resolve a known
     duplicate, it is there so that a URL reached with a tracking parameter, a
     trailing-slash variant or through the preview host consolidates onto one
     address instead of competing with itself. #}
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ page.url | absoluteUrl }}">
{#- Emitted on every deploy that is not the production branch, and on nothing
    else. The production host carries NO robots meta tag at all, which is the
    safe shape: there is no state to get stuck in. See src/_data/deploy.js. -#}
{#- `noindex: true` in a page's front matter is the OTHER way in, and it is
    about a page rather than about a deploy. An internal tool like /yelp-map/
    must carry the directive on production too, where deploy.indexable is true
    and this block would otherwise emit nothing.

    OR, NOT A SEPARATE BLOCK. One tag, two reasons to emit it, so the two can
    never both fire and write it twice. A page opting in on a preview build is
    already covered and stays covered. -#}
{%- if not deploy.indexable or noindex %}
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
{%- endif %}

  {# Images come from the CDN, so warm the connection before the first request. #}
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://cdn.circulationstudio.com" crossorigin>
  {# A page names its LCP image in front matter and it gets preloaded. Without
     this the hero image is not discovered until the parser reaches it. #}
  {% if preloadImage %}
  <link rel="preload" as="image" href="{{ site.cdn }}{{ preloadImage }}" fetchpriority="high">
  {% endif %}
  <script type="module" src="/src/js/main.js"></script>

  {# JSON-LD. Reads site.nap, the same object the colophon renders, so the
     encoded NAP and the visible NAP cannot disagree. See partials/schema.njk
     for what is deliberately absent from the graph and why. #}
  {% include "partials/schema.njk" %}
</head>
<body>
  {# Hand-rolled rather than Tailwind's sr-only + focus:not-sr-only pair. That
     pair returns the link to STATIC flow on focus, and below 1120px the bar
     is fixed and always present, so the focused link landed behind it. See
     .cs-skip in masthead.css. #}
  <a class="cs-skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

  {% include "partials/masthead.njk" %}

  <main id="main">
    {{ content | safe }}
  </main>

  {% include "partials/footer.njk" %}
</body>
</html>
